//? Title: MNIST CNN: Image Features and an Explicit Adam Loop
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A handwritten 28×28 digit must be mapped to one of ten classes. A small CNN shares local
filters before learning a dense readout. We inspect actual MNIST inputs and intermediate
shapes, then execute a short, visible minibatch Adam run with validation-only checkpoint selection.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.1_fundamentals/cnn_mnist.cpp`.

> The method

The shared model applies SAME 3×3 Conv(16)-ReLU, 2×2 max-pooling, SAME Conv(32)-ReLU,
2×2 pooling, Dense(64)-ReLU and ten logits. Spatial sizes go 28→14→7. A convolution with
Cin input channels, Cout outputs and k×k support learns k² Cin Cout+Cout scalars.
The dense hidden layer learns (7·7·32)·64+64. Total parameters are 105866.

$$
L=\frac1B\sum_i\left[-z_{i,y_i}+\operatorname{logsumexp}_k z_{ik}\right]
+\frac{10^{-4}}2\sum_{W\text{ kernels}}\|W\|_F^2.
$$
\alttext(The mean sparse softmax cross entropy receives an L2 penalty on convolution and dense kernels, excluding biases.)

Autograd computes parameter gradients; the explicit Adam optimizer updates all parameters
created before its construction. The training loop, batching, loss and checkpoint selection
remain in the report. Validation NLL chooses an epoch; test rows do not influence selection.
Convolution work is O(B Ho Wo k² Cin Cout) per layer. The report uses 512 fitting rows,
128 validation rows and 128 original test rows over three epochs, rather than claim the
full 55000/5000/10000 benchmark. It requires cached MNIST under DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR or the
standard user dataset cache and performs no download.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/cnn_mnist_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/cnn_mnist_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/cnn_mnist_concept.tikz > build/cnn_mnist_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/cnn_mnist_concept.svg build/cnn_mnist_concept.dvi > build/cnn_mnist_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
